.TH "phosh-session" "" "" ""
.SH "نام (NAME)"
phosh-session \- Session startup script for phosh
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.nf
\fBphosh\-session\fP [OPTIONS...]
.fi
.sp
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
\fBphosh\-session\fP is the script to startup phosh including required
components like the Wayland compositor \fBphoc\fP and an on screen
keyboard like \fBstevia\fP or \fBsqueekboard\fP\&. The script is rarely invoked by a
user but rather activated by a display manager or systemd unit. However it\(aqs
perfectly valid to e.g. log into a tty and run \fBphosh\-session\fP to bring up
phosh and needed components.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
Print help and exit
.TP
.B \fB\-\-version\fP
Print version and exit
.UNINDENT
.SH "فایل‌های پیکربندی (CONFIGURATION FILES)"
.sp
The session script looks at the following configuration files:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB/usr/share/phosh/phoc.ini\fP: Configuration passed to the compositor
.IP \(bu 2
\fB/etc/phosh/phoc.ini\fP: Used instead of the above if present
.UNINDENT
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.sp
\fBphosh\-session\fP honors the following environment variables:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWLR_BACKENDS\fP: The backends the wlroots library should use when phoc launches. See
\%<https://\:gitlab\:.freedesktop\:.org/\:wlroots/\:wlroots/\:-/\:blob/\:master/\:docs/\:env_vars\:.md>
.UNINDENT
.sp
For debugging purposes you can put environment variables into
\fB~/.phoshdebug\fP which is read at session startup.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.sp
\fBphosh(1)\fP \fBphoc(1)\fP \fBphoc.ini(5)\fP \fBphosh\-osk\-stevia(1)\fP
.\" End of generated man page.
